        "subject": "[Weekly Review] Update your LinkedIn Analytics in Google Sheets",
        "message": "=<h2>Weekly LinkedIn Analytics Reminder</h2>\n\n<p>Hey Abdullah — time to log this week's LinkedIn post performance.</p>\n\n<p>Open your <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1IwKjyPCJ0tGpFpRceUxQwGACf9Uk0IZoSsoXqJyAAjY\">Google Sheet → 📊 LinkedIn Analytics tab</a> and fill in reactions, comments, and impressions for each post below.</p>\n\n<h3>Posts from this week:</h3>\n<table border='1' cellpadding='8' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:collapse;width:100%'>\n  <tr style='background:#f0f4ff'>\n    <th>Date</th><th>Title</th><th>Category</th><th>URL</th>\n  </tr>\n  {{ $input.all().filter(i => !i.json.noPosts).map(i => `<tr><td>${i.json.date}</td><td>${i.json.postTitle}</td><td>${i.json.category}</td><td><a href='${i.json.linkedInUrl}'>View Post</a></td></tr>`).join('') }}\n</table>\n\n<br>\n<p>Tracking which topics get the most reactions helps you post more of what works.</p>\n<p style='color:#666;font-size:12px'>Sent automatically every Monday by your n8n workflow.</p>",
